      <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Quick Summary: What Time Zone is the UK In?</h3>
      <p>
        The United Kingdom operates on <strong>Greenwich Mean Time (GMT, UTC+0)</strong> during the winter and shifts to <strong>British Summer Time (BST, UTC+1)</strong> during the summer when Daylight Saving Time (DST) is active. The transition to BST occurs on the <strong>last Sunday of March</strong> (clocks go forward 1 hour at 01:00 UTC), and the return to GMT occurs on the <strong>last Sunday of October</strong> (clocks go back 1 hour at 02:00 BST).
      </p>
      <p>
        While mainland Great Britain and Northern Ireland follow this dual-offset pattern, the UK's 14 Overseas Territories and Crown Dependencies span 9 different time zones across the globe, ranging from UTC-8 in the Pitcairn Islands to UTC+6 in the British Indian Ocean Territory.
      </p>
