          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, March 29 (01:00 UTC to 02:00 BST)</td>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, October 25 (02:00 BST to 01:00 GMT)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">2027</td>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, March 28 (01:00 UTC to 02:00 BST)</td>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, October 31 (02:00 BST to 01:00 GMT)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">2028</td>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, March 26 (01:00 UTC to 02:00 BST)</td>
          <td style="padding: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);">Sunday, October 29 (02:00 BST to 01:00 GMT)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      For more details on seasonal clock adjustments globally, see our dedicated <a href="/daylight-saving-time-explained/">Daylight Saving Time guide</a> and <a href="/est-vs-edt/">EST vs EDT guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4 -->
  <section id="uk-overseas-territories" class="content-section">
    <h2>4. UK Overseas Territories &amp; Crown Dependencies</h2>
    <p>
      While the home nations (England, Scotland, Wales, Northern Ireland) observe GMT and BST, the British Crown exercises sovereignty over 14 Overseas Territories and 3 Crown Dependencies. Collectively, these territories span 9 distinct time zones around the globe:
    </p>
    <table class="data-table" style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--line);">
